"hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1310,"It is narrated by Sayyiduna Habib ibn Abi Thabit (may Allah have mercy on him) that he liked that when a person speaks, he should not direct his attention towards any one individual, but rather address the gathering in a general manner.
Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1310 | Arabic Hadith: 1310"
1311,"It is narrated by Ibn Abi Hazil (may Allah have mercy on him) that Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) went with one of his companions to visit a sick person. When they entered the house, the people of the house began looking here and there. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to them: ""By Allah! If both your eyes were gouged out, it would be far better for you.""
Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1311 | Arabic Hadith: 1311"
1312,"It is narrated by Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that some people from Iraq came to Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he noticed a gold necklace around the neck of one of their slave-girls, whereupon they began looking at one another. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""Your eyes are exceedingly sharp at seeing evil.""
Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1312 | Arabic Hadith: 1312"
1313,"It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: There is no good in idle talk.
Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1313 | Arabic Hadith: 1313"
1314,"It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The worst and most wicked people of my Ummah are those who talk excessively, those who engage in boastful and ostentatious conversation, and those who speak with their mouths wide open. And the best people of my Ummah are those who are the most excellent in character.""
Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1314 | Arabic Hadith: 1314"
1315,"It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among the wicked is the one who practises duplicity — he says one thing to one group and goes to another group and says something else.""
Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1315 | Arabic Hadith: 1315"
1316,"Sayyidunā ʿAmmār ibn Yāṣir (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhumā) narrates that he heard the Prophet (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) saying: ""Whoever is two-faced (a hypocrite) in this world, on the Day of Resurrection he will have two tongues of fire."" Then a stout, heavy-built man passed by, and the Prophet (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: ""He is one of them.""

Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1316 | Arabic Hadith: 1316"
1317,"Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless
him and grant him peace, said, ""The person who is strong is not strong
because he can knock people down. The person who is strong is the one who
controls himself when he is angry."""
1318,"Ibn 'Umar said, ""There is nothing that is swallowed greater with
Allah in reward than a slave of Allah who swallows and contains his rancour
out of desire for the pleasure of Allah."""
1319,"Sulayman ibn Surad said, ""Two men abused one another in the presence of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and one of them began to get angry and his face got red. The Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, looked at him and said, 'I know some words that, if he says them, will remove this from him. They are:""I seek refuge with Allah from the Accursed Shaytan.""' The man went to that man and said, 'Do you know what he said? He said, ""I seek refuge with Allah from the Accursed Shaytan.""' The man retorted. 'Do you think me mad?'"""
1320,"Ibn 'Abbas said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him
and grant him peace, said, ' Teach and make it easy. Teach and make it
easy.' three times. He went on, 'When you are angry, be silent' twice."""
1321,"'Ali was heard to say to Ibn al-Kawwa', ""Do you know what the
first one said? 'Loving the one you love is an easy matter. It may be that
one day he will be the one you hate. Hating the one who hate is an easy
matter. It may be that one day he will be the one you love.'"""
